From: Xperia Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:25:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: use pixel RCG ops for MSM8x60 DSI

The generic table-driven RCG operations reject the panel's 69.673 MHz
pixel rate because dsi1_pixel_src has no discrete frequency table. This
clock is an M/N pixel divider fed by the DSI PLL, matching the hardware
model handled by clk_rcg_pixel_ops. Use those operations and permit parent
rate propagation so the DSI host can derive the pixel clock from its PLL.

Signed-off-by: Xperia Hikari Linux Project <hikari-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
@@ -694,7 +694,8 @@ static struct clk_rcg dsi1_pixel_src = {
 			.name = "dsi1_pixel_src",
 			.parent_data = mmcc_pxo_dsi2_dsi1,
 			.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(mmcc_pxo_dsi2_dsi1),
-			.ops = &clk_rcg_ops,
+			.ops = &clk_rcg_pixel_ops,
+			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 		},
 	},
 };
-- 
2.43.0
